{"_v":1,"id":"amelie-a-new-musical-2017","cs":47,"rc":7,"bd":{"positive":1,"mixed":1,"negative":5},"rv":[{"cn":"Marilyn Stasio","o":"Variety","s":77,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://variety.com/2016/legit/reviews/amelie-a-new-musical-review-1201945368/","d":"2017-04-04","q":"This effervescent musical adaptation of the beloved French film manages to capture both the whimsical spirit and emotional depth of the original, though it sometimes struggles under the weight of its own theatrical ambitions."},{"cn":"Adam Feldman","o":"Time Out New York","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.timeout.com/newyork/theater/amelie-a-new-musical","d":"2017-04-03","q":"The show has a sweetness that is hard to resist, even when its whimsy occasionally crosses the line into preciousness."},{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":45,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/2017/04/03/theater/amelie-musical-broadway-review-phillipa-soo.html","d":"2017-04-04","q":"“Amélie” the musical seems to have no nationality, or sensibility, to call its own."},{"cn":"Peter Marks","o":"The Washington Post","s":38,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/entertainment/theater_dance/review-amelie-a-new-musical-needs-more-than-whimsy-to-succeed/2017/04/04/8b0c6e7e-196a-11e7-9887-1a5314b56a08_story.html","d":"2017-04-04","q":"What's missing is the theatrical magic that might compensate for a score that feels more workmanlike than wonderful."},{"cn":"Jesse Green","o":"Vulture","s":30,"b":"Pan","t":1,"u":"https://www.vulture.com/2017/04/theater-review-amelie-a-new-musical.html","d":"2017-04-04","q":"The musical version of Amélie is so determined to be enchanting that it becomes exhausting instead."},{"cn":"Terry Teachout","o":"The Wall Street Journal","s":25,"b":"Pan","t":1,"u":"https://www.wsj.com/articles/amelie-a-new-musical-review-whimsy-without-magic-1491602403","d":"2017-04-07","q":"The problem with 'Amélie' is that it feels more like a theme-park ride than a musical—and not a very good ride at that."},{"cn":"Casey Curtis","o":"Front Row Center","s":45,"b":"Negative","t":3,"u":"https://thefrontrowcenter.com/2017/04/a-homily-for-amelie/","d":"2017-04-08","q":"But overall this show is a lesson in messing with the sacred."}],"au":{"score":63,"designation":"Disliking","sources":{"mz":{"s":63,"c":184,"sr":3.1}}},"ta":"219 W 48th St, New York, NY 10036","pd":"2017-03-09","ca":[{"n":"Adam Chanler-Berat","r":"Nino"},{"n":"Phillipa Soo","r":"Amélie"},{"n":"Tony Sheldon","r":"Dufayel"},{"n":"David Andino","r":"Blind Beggar"},{"n":"Randy Blair","r":"Hipolito"},{"n":"Heath Calvert","r":"Lucien"},{"n":"Alison Cimmet","r":"Amandine"},{"n":"Savvy Crawford","r":"Young Amélie"},{"n":"Manoel Felciano","r":"Raphael"},{"n":"Harriett D. Foy","r":"Suzanne"},{"n":"Alyse Alan Louis","r":"Georgette"},{"n":"Maria-Christina Oliveras","r":"Gina"},{"n":"Paul Whitty","r":"Joseph"}]}